/// This API generates label files for an inbound order using an **asynchronous Long-Running Operation (LRO)**. The inbound order must be shipped or in a later eligible status and must not be canceled.  **Format applicability** * `carton_label_format` controls the carton or pallet label layout only when `print_items` includes `CARTON_PALLET_LABEL`. * `barcode_format` controls the goods-barcode label layout only when `print_items` includes `FBT_BARCODE`.  The selected `print_items` and both resolved format values are part of the print task identifier, so keep the same selections in every polling request.  **Workflow** 1. **Initiate.** Send a request with the child inbound `order_id` and the desired `print_items`. The API returns `PROCESSING` while the label file is being generated; a completed task for the same request values may return `SUCCESS` immediately. 2. **Poll.** If `task_status` is `PROCESSING`, repeat the request with the same `order_id`, `print_items`, `carton_label_format`, and `barcode_format` values. Poll every 3–5 seconds. 3. **Complete.** When `task_status` is `SUCCESS`, `download_url` contains the generated ZIP file.
